# Deferred manual testing (all projects)

## Principle

During implementation, **the agent runs automated verification itself**. **The user runs manual browser/UI testing once** — at **solution completion** (milestone in `task.md`), not after every feature or PR-sized change.

**Automate first:** Manual testing is **only** for what cannot be automated after a genuine attempt. The agent **must try to automate every test** before adding it to `MANUAL_TEST.md` or asking the user to verify anything.

No back-and-forth: *"open localhost and click through"* mid-build.

## Automate first — manual only as last resort

For **every** verification need, follow this order:

1. **Try to automate** — script, smoke test, pytest, API/CLI check, headless HTTP, fixture CSV, mock payment webhook, etc.
2. **If automated** — run it during build; do **not** duplicate the same step in `MANUAL_TEST.md` for the user.
3. **If not automatable** — add to `MANUAL_TEST.md` with a one-line **Why not automated** (e.g. "Streamlit widget layout", "subjective AI tone", "real Paystack live card", "WhatsApp app on physical phone").
4. **User runs manual steps once** at v1 sign-off — **only** the items that remain after step 1–3.

The user should **never** manually repeat a check the agent could have scripted. When in doubt, automate.

## During build (agent)

**Do automatically** (without asking the user to interact in the web UI):

- Unit/smoke/integration scripts the agent can run (`pytest`, `test_*_flow.py`, import checks, `py_compile`)
- CLI/API checks, CSV/export logic, HTTP health on localhost if needed for automation
- Start dev servers in background **only** when required for automated checks — not as a handoff to the user
- Report outcomes as: automated pass/fail + what remains in the manual checklist

**Do not** (until solution-complete milestone):

- Ask the user to open a browser, upload files in Streamlit, or click UI controls as the default next step
- Treat manual UI verification as part of the incremental dev loop
- End every response with "please manually test in the browser" unless the user explicitly asks for a mid-build UI check

## Manual test file (agent maintains; user runs once)

For each active product/app folder, maintain **`MANUAL_TEST.md`** (same folder as the app, e.g. `post-wedding-comms-pack/MANUAL_TEST.md`):

- **Only** steps that failed the automate-first rule above
- Each manual item should note **Why not automated** where non-obvious
- **Append** as features land (prerequisites, UI flows, edge cases, sign-off checkbox)
- **One end-to-end session** — not scattered prompts in chat
- Include: env setup, run command, ordered steps, expected results, pass/fail notes section
- Move steps out of chat into this file instead of re-asking the user repeatedly

If no `MANUAL_TEST.md` exists yet when manual steps are identified, create the template when starting substantive work on that product — still **do not** ask the user to execute it until sign-off.

## When the user tests manually

Only when **all** of the following are true:

1. **Solution-complete milestone** is defined in `.cursor/rules/task.md` (e.g. "Post-Wedding Comms Pack v1 = P0 + P1")
2. **Automate-first exhausted** — agent has run all scriptable tests; remaining items are documented in `MANUAL_TEST.md` with reasons
3. Automated checks for that milestone are green (or failures documented)
4. Agent explicitly says: **"Ready for single manual pass — run `MANUAL_TEST.md`"** (listing what automation already covered)

Mid-build exceptions: user explicitly requests a UI check, or a blocker cannot be diagnosed without human eyes (state why; keep scope minimal).

## End-of-conversation menus

Default recommended actions should **not** be "open browser and test" during build. Prefer: continue next automated task, update `MANUAL_TEST.md`, run smoke tests, or advance `task.md` phases.

Offer **one** manual-test menu item only at/near solution-complete milestone.

## v1 sign-off (definition of done)

Before the single manual pass, `task.md` should name what "complete" means (features + phases). Manual UI pass is the **last** gate before staging/commit/push for launch — not a recurring gate.
